{"Name":"Execute Custom Query","Description":"Execute a custom hunting query in Microsoft 365 Defender.","Script":"from ScriptResult import EXECUTION_STATE_COMPLETED, EXECUTION_STATE_FAILED\nfrom SiemplifyAction import SiemplifyAction\nfrom SiemplifyUtils import output_handler\n\nfrom TIPCommon.extraction import extract_configuration_param, extract_action_param\nfrom TIPCommon.transformation import construct_csv\n\nfrom constants import (\n    INTEGRATION_NAME,\n    INTEGRATION_DISPLAY_NAME,\n    EXECUTE_CUSTOM_QUERY_SCRIPT_NAME,\n    DEFAULT_RESULTS_LIMIT,\n    LOGIN_API_ROOT_DEFAULT,\n    GRAPH_API_ROOT_DEFAULT,\n)\nfrom Microsoft365DefenderManager import Microsoft365DefenderManager\n\nTABLE_NAME = \"Results\"\n\n\n@output_handler\ndef main():\n    siemplify = SiemplifyAction()\n    siemplify.script_name = EXECUTE_CUSTOM_QUERY_SCRIPT_NAME\n    siemplify.LOGGER.info(\"----------------- Main - Param Init -----------------\")\n\n    login_api_root = extract_configuration_param(\n        siemplify,\n        provider_name=INTEGRATION_NAME,\n        param_name=\"Login API Root\",\n        is_mandatory=True,\n        default_value=LOGIN_API_ROOT_DEFAULT,\n        print_value=True,\n    )\n    graph_api_root = extract_configuration_param(\n        siemplify,\n        provider_name=INTEGRATION_NAME,\n        param_name=\"Graph API Root\",\n        is_mandatory=True,\n        default_value=GRAPH_API_ROOT_DEFAULT,\n        print_value=True,\n    )\n    api_root = extract_configuration_param(\n        siemplify,\n        provider_name=INTEGRATION_NAME,\n        param_name=\"API Root\",\n        is_mandatory=True,\n        print_value=True,\n    )\n    tenant_id = extract_configuration_param(\n        siemplify,\n        provider_name=INTEGRATION_NAME,\n        param_name=\"Tenant ID\",\n        is_mandatory=True,\n        print_value=True,\n    )\n    client_id = extract_configuration_param(\n        siemplify,\n        provider_name=INTEGRATION_NAME,\n        param_name=\"Client ID\",\n        is_mandatory=True,\n        print_value=True,\n        remove_whitespaces=False,\n    )\n    client_secret = extract_configuration_param(\n        siemplify,\n        provider_name=INTEGRATION_NAME,\n        param_name=\"Client Secret\",\n        is_mandatory=True,\n        remove_whitespaces=False,\n    )\n    verify_ssl = extract_configuration_param(\n        siemplify,\n        provider_name=INTEGRATION_NAME,\n        param_name=\"Verify SSL\",\n        input_type=bool,\n        is_mandatory=True,\n        print_value=True,\n    )\n\n    # Action parameters\n    custom_query = extract_action_param(\n        siemplify, param_name=\"Query\", print_value=True, is_mandatory=True\n    )\n    limit = extract_action_param(\n        siemplify,\n        param_name=\"Max Results To Return\",\n        input_type=int,\n        print_value=True,\n        default_value=DEFAULT_RESULTS_LIMIT,\n    )\n\n    siemplify.LOGGER.info(\"----------------- Main - Started -----------------\")\n\n    result = False\n    status = EXECUTION_STATE_COMPLETED\n\n    try:\n        if limit < 1:\n            raise Exception('\"Max Results To Return\" must be greater than 0.')\n\n        manager = Microsoft365DefenderManager(\n            api_root=api_root,\n            tenant_id=tenant_id,\n            client_id=client_id,\n            client_secret=client_secret,\n            verify_ssl=verify_ssl,\n            microsoft_graph_url=graph_api_root,\n            siemplify=siemplify,\n            login_api_root=login_api_root,\n        )\n        devices, query_string = manager.search_for_devices(\n            custom_query=custom_query, limit=limit\n        )\n\n        if devices:\n            result = True\n            siemplify.result.add_data_table(\n                TABLE_NAME, construct_csv([device.to_csv() for device in devices])\n            )\n            siemplify.result.add_result_json([device.to_json() for device in devices])\n            output_message = (\n                f'Successfully executed query \"{query_string}\" in {INTEGRATION_DISPLAY_NAME}'\n                if query_string\n                else f\"Successfully executed query in {INTEGRATION_DISPLAY_NAME}\"\n            )\n        else:\n            output_message = (\n                f'No data was found for the query \"{query_string}\" in {INTEGRATION_DISPLAY_NAME}'\n                if query_string\n                else f\"No data was found for the query in {INTEGRATION_DISPLAY_NAME}\"\n            )\n\n    except Exception as e:\n        siemplify.LOGGER.error(\n            f\"General error performing action {EXECUTE_CUSTOM_QUERY_SCRIPT_NAME}\"\n        )\n        siemplify.LOGGER.exception(e)\n        status = EXECUTION_STATE_FAILED\n        output_message = (\n            f'Error executing action \"{EXECUTE_CUSTOM_QUERY_SCRIPT_NAME}\" Reason: {e}'\n        )\n\n    siemplify.LOGGER.info(\"----------------- Main - Finished -----------------\")\n    siemplify.LOGGER.info(f\"Status: {status}\")\n    siemplify.LOGGER.info(f\"Result: {result}\")\n    siemplify.LOGGER.info(f\"Output Message: {output_message}\")\n\n    siemplify.end(output_message, result, status)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n","IntegrationIdentifier":"Microsoft365DefenderBeta","ScriptResultName":"is_success","DynamicResultsMetadata":[{"ResultName":"JsonResult","ResultExample":"[{\"Timestamp\":\"2021-04-12T07:25:00Z\",\"AlertId\":\"fa7a318954-6c4c-eaab-xxx-xxxxxxxxxx\",\"Title\":\"CC_Sensitive information\",\"Category\":\"InitialAccess\",\"Severity\":\"Medium\",\"ServiceSource\":\"Microsoft Defender for Office 365\",\"DetectionSource\":\"Microsoft Defender for Office 365\",\"AttackTechniques\":\"\"}]","ShowResult":true}],"Creator":"admin","IsEnabled":true,"IsCustom":true,"AiGenerated":false,"IsSystem":false,"Version":0.0,"TimeoutSeconds":600,"IsAsync":null,"AsyncPollingIntervalInSeconds":300,"TotalIntervalTimeoutForAsyncInSeconds":3600,"Parameters":[{"CustomActionId":0,"IsMandatory":true,"DefaultValue":"","Description":"Specify the query that needs to be executed. Use this parameter to provide |where clauses. Note: Note: you don't need to provide a limiting (\"top\" keyword).","Name":"Query","Value":"","Type":0,"OptionalValues":null,"OptionalValuesJson":null},{"CustomActionId":0,"IsMandatory":false,"DefaultValue":"50","Description":"Specify how many results to return. Default: 50.","Name":"Max Results To Return","Value":"50","Type":0,"OptionalValues":null,"OptionalValuesJson":null}],"DefaultResultValue":null,"PythonVersion":"None","ActionType":1,"SimulationData":{"Entities":null},"SimulationDataJson":null,"AICategories":["Enrichment"],"OutcomeCategories":["Search Events"],"AIDescription":"### General Description\nExecutes a custom Kusto Query Language (KQL) hunting query against Microsoft 365 Defender's advanced hunting data. This action allows security analysts to perform flexible, ad-hoc searches across various data tables (like DeviceProcessEvents, EmailEvents, etc.) within the Microsoft 365 Defender environment. The results are returned as a structured data table and a JSON object for further automation steps.\n\n### Flow Description\n1. **Initialization**: The action retrieves connection settings and action parameters (`Query` and `Max Results To Return`).\n2. **Query Preparation**: It appends a `| limit` clause to the user-provided query to ensure the result set size is controlled.\n3. **API Execution**: It first attempts to execute the query using the Microsoft Graph API (`/beta/security/runHuntingQuery`). If the Graph API call fails due to a permission error (403), it automatically falls back to the Legacy Microsoft 365 Defender API (`/api/advancedhunting/run`).\n4. **Data Processing**: The raw response is parsed into a list of results.\n5. **Output Generation**: If data is found, it populates a SOAR data table named 'Results' and adds the raw JSON to the action's result object. If no data is found, it reports a successful execution with a 'No data found' message.\n\n### Additional Notes\nThe action automatically appends a limit clause, so the 'top' or 'limit' keywords are not required in the input string.","AiShortDescription":"Executes a custom Kusto Query Language (KQL) hunting query against Microsoft 365 Defender's advanced hunting data.","ParametersDescription":"| Parameter | Type | Mandatory | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Query | String | Yes | Specify the query that needs to be executed. Use this parameter to provide \\|where clauses. Note: you don't need to provide a limiting (\"top\" keyword). |\n| Max Results To Return | Integer | No | Specify how many results to return. Default: 50. |","ImpactAnalysisActionsMetadata":null,"EntityTypes":[]}